.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1004 AM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026

VFR at all terminals this morning with onshore winds forecast to
increase through the afternoon before easing after sunset.
However, the forecast wind speeds will be less than previous days.
Moderate confidence for the return of stratus over the Bay Area
terminals tonight with higher confidence for the Monterey Bay
terminals. Onshore winds increase once again by Tuesday afternoon.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Onshore winds are forecast to increase
throughout the afternoon with gusts up to 25 kt before gradually
easing late in the night. Moderate confidence for stratus at
around 1500 feet to arrive around 10Z Tuesday before scattering
out by 17Z. However, the HRRR does not suggest ceilings make it
over SFO. Thus, leaning more on the NBM and GFS-LAMP guidance.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Onshore winds increase this
afternoon and gradually diminish after sunset. Moderate to high
confidence for IFR/MVFR ceilings to return late this evening and
into Tuesday

