.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 436 AM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026

A few patches of coastal stratus have developed overnight. North
to northeast breezes have developed in the higher terrain. Offshore
winds will diminish by late morning or early afternoon and return
to diurnally breezy onshore winds in the afternoon and evening. A
surface to lower level trough of low pressure will develop along
the north Central Coast Tuesday through Tuesday night. Surface to
lower level troughing will expand to include the Bay Area Wednesday
through Thursday. This will bring higher humidity with good recoveries
from sea level to lower elevations to around 2500 feet, however above
this elevation especially along the higher ridgetops thermal ridging
and much lower humidity will persist during mid-week.

As such, areas above the marine layer often experience nocturnal
drying that will likely continue through early this upcoming week.

